[SPEAKER_15]: Hey there, this is Amy from the city of Medford.

99
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:39,512
[SPEAKER_14]: Denny Freezer, if you'd like to introduce yourself.

100
00:03:40,613 --> 00:03:47,238
[SPEAKER_14]: If you have trouble with your camera or your microphone and you can't, you can type into the chat and introduce yourself there.

101
00:03:51,512 --> 00:03:53,573
[SPEAKER_00]: Hi, can everybody hear me?

102
00:03:53,633 --> 00:03:55,014
[SPEAKER_00]: I just unmuted myself.

103
00:03:55,074 --> 00:03:55,274
[SPEAKER_06]: Yes.

104
00:03:55,894 --> 00:03:57,455
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm brand new to Medford.

105
00:03:57,535 --> 00:04:02,298
[SPEAKER_00]: I haven't even moved in yet, but I saw that you had a meeting and I wanted to watch what's going on.

106
00:04:02,318 --> 00:04:06,260
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm a lifelong cyclist, so I'll just keep quiet and watch tonight.

107
00:04:07,381 --> 00:04:08,321
[SPEAKER_14]: Awesome, welcome.

108
00:04:08,341 --> 00:04:09,382
[SPEAKER_00]: Welcome.

109
00:04:12,503 --> 00:04:14,665
[SPEAKER_14]: Great, so we have a few announcements.

110
00:04:15,762 --> 00:04:17,243
[SPEAKER_14]: Most of these should be fairly brief.

111
00:04:18,283 --> 00:04:30,629
[SPEAKER_14]: The first is that there is a message from Amber Christopherson that was really short notice, but they are, that she's of Mystic River Watershed Association.

112
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:40,473
[SPEAKER_14]: They're exploring the idea of creating a shared use path from High Street up to Mystic Valley Parkway, up to the, up Mystic Valley Parkway to the Tri-Community Greenway.

113
00:04:41,294 --> 00:04:42,814
[SPEAKER_14]: We've discussed that previously.

114
00:04:44,535 --> 00:04:54,458
[SPEAKER_14]: They have gotten the go ahead from DCR to apply for a mass trails grant for a feasibility study, and they wanted a letter of support on behalf of MBAC.

115
00:04:54,858 --> 00:05:01,320
[SPEAKER_14]: So I took the action of sending that letter of support on our behalf.

116
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:08,642
[SPEAKER_14]: The timeline was pretty short, and I don't think anybody is going to complain about that.

117
00:05:10,584 --> 00:05:21,802
[SPEAKER_14]: Next thing is the Office of Planning, Development and Sustainability has a website, and it would be really nice if there was a little more information on that website about

118
00:05:22,893 --> 00:05:28,596
[SPEAKER_14]: how to get around in Medford without using your car or with using your car a little less.

119
00:05:29,477 --> 00:05:42,285
[SPEAKER_14]: And I met a little while ago with Ellery Klein from Walk Medford and Gaston Fiore in doing double duty and discussed a number of things that can be added to that website.

120
00:05:42,305 --> 00:05:46,988
[SPEAKER_14]: For starters, we'll just have some really basic information about the mechanics of

121
00:05:47,828 --> 00:05:56,192
[SPEAKER_14]: finding a good bike route and how to like follow a bike route that you have saved on your phone in some way.

122
00:05:57,272 --> 00:06:14,520
[SPEAKER_14]: Some of the places you might go looking for good bike routes, nothing too complicated, but I think this is also a good opportunity to think about if there's more in-depth information we might want to add to our own website, including maybe more

123
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:35,698
[SPEAKER_14]: max or more in depth information about other stuff about just getting around bike by bike in Medford or using a bike as a multimodal method in combination with blue bikes when we eventually get them or in combination with using your own bike etc.

124
00:06:36,438 --> 00:06:57,365
[SPEAKER_14]: So just something to think about, even if not all of the gory details go on the website of the Office of Planning, Development and Sustainability, if we have a lot more in-depth information that we want to add to over time, then linking to the Medford Bikes website would be a good way to tie into that.

125
00:06:59,545 --> 00:07:07,548
[SPEAKER_14]: So that's an effort that's ongoing and I will update you when there's more information.

126
00:07:08,468 --> 00:07:10,449
[SPEAKER_14]: Are there any other updates or announcements?

127
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:19,112
[SPEAKER_05]: One thing I should probably request is just that we do an approval of the minutes.

128
00:07:20,185 --> 00:07:22,866
[SPEAKER_14]: You're right, and I missed that.

129
00:07:24,046 --> 00:07:27,767
[SPEAKER_14]: Do we have a... Has everybody looked at the minutes?

130
00:07:28,267 --> 00:07:38,729
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, before you motion, I made a couple of edits about an hour ago, just to the dates on the Clippership Connector and the League of American Bicyclists certification.

131
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:46,871
[SPEAKER_13]: Does anybody have any other additions or comments?

132
00:07:52,888 --> 00:07:54,249
[SPEAKER_13]: Do we have a motion to approve the minutes?

133
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:58,911
[SPEAKER_03]: Seconded.

134
00:08:00,212 --> 00:08:00,793
[SPEAKER_14]: All in favor?

135
00:08:02,013 --> 00:08:02,153
[SPEAKER_06]: Aye.

136
00:08:03,074 --> 00:08:03,294
[SPEAKER_06]: Yes.

137
00:08:04,054 --> 00:08:04,595
[SPEAKER_14]: All opposed?

138
00:08:07,416 --> 00:08:08,277
[SPEAKER_14]: Minutes are approved.

139
00:08:09,858 --> 00:08:11,219
[SPEAKER_14]: Do we have any other announcements?

140
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,021
[SPEAKER_03]: Emily?

141
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:18,703
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, can I just say, do we need to announce that we have a quorum?

142
00:08:19,703 --> 00:08:26,629
[SPEAKER_03]: just for formality, I forget whether we do that each month.

143
00:08:26,749 --> 00:08:29,411
[SPEAKER_14]: It doesn't hurt to point out that we definitely do have a quorum.

144
00:08:31,893 --> 00:08:34,135
[SPEAKER_14]: We did the roll call and we were not missing very many.

145
00:08:34,355 --> 00:08:36,036
[SPEAKER_14]: So I think we're covered.

146
00:08:36,056 --> 00:08:43,182
[SPEAKER_14]: Are there other announcements before we go on?

147
00:08:48,309 --> 00:08:56,753
[SPEAKER_14]: Good, so the next thing on the agenda is the Salem Street bike lanes that were approved by the Traffic Commission recently.

148
00:08:58,094 --> 00:09:02,556
[SPEAKER_14]: Amy, if you are here and would you like to say anything about that?

149
00:09:05,198 --> 00:09:05,538
[SPEAKER_14]: Go ahead.

150
00:09:06,478 --> 00:09:07,079
[SPEAKER_15]: Sure, I can.

151
