00:17:52,872 --> 00:17:55,194
[SPEAKER_15]: I don't know.

233
00:17:55,214 --> 00:17:56,255
[SPEAKER_15]: Sounds like someone's TV.

234
00:17:58,356 --> 00:18:02,179
[SPEAKER_14]: We are also right after this spot, the bike lane ends entirely.

235
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:10,564
[SPEAKER_14]: So we also need to think about how that termination looks visually.

236
00:18:10,584 --> 00:18:16,809
[SPEAKER_14]: A lot of times when they have kind of the angle dotted line that angles off to the right at the end of a bike lane,

237
00:18:17,965 --> 00:18:23,308
[SPEAKER_14]: We know that the dotted line means that the bicyclists are going to cross the dotted line and be in the travel lane.

238
00:18:23,708 --> 00:18:32,433
[SPEAKER_14]: But what it visually looks like is that the bicyclists shrink down to being six inches wide and they turn into riding on the fog line or something.

239
00:18:34,174 --> 00:18:44,779
[SPEAKER_14]: And I think there are other ways that make it look like two streams of traffic are merging rather than like some people that used to be on your right-hand side are now disappearing.

240
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:49,281
[SPEAKER_14]: At least can we get sheriffs there?

241
00:18:49,301 --> 00:18:52,001
[SPEAKER_07]: Not enough.

242
00:18:54,582 --> 00:18:58,523
[SPEAKER_07]: I agree, but it's, you know, it's better than just having the bike lane disappear.

243
00:18:59,163 --> 00:19:12,547
[SPEAKER_14]: Well, some things that I think we also discussed are like having the bike lane turns into kind of like blocks that then lead into the middle of the travel lane and then it disappears.

244
00:19:13,087 --> 00:19:14,868
[SPEAKER_14]: So then it's really clear that there's something

245
00:19:16,485 --> 00:19:20,546
[SPEAKER_14]: There's something guiding you, directing people that direction.

246
00:19:21,687 --> 00:19:30,709
[SPEAKER_14]: And then it just is clear to everybody involved that two streams of traffic have to merge, not that one of them just goes away.

247
00:19:30,729 --> 00:19:38,872
[SPEAKER_15]: Does that make sense?

248
00:19:40,433 --> 00:19:46,586
[SPEAKER_09]: The other comment that I had at the track question meeting was that if there's room for it.

