[SPEAKER_14]: You can ride across Medford pretty quickly in any direction.

539
00:47:51,996 --> 00:47:53,236
[SPEAKER_14]: There's just not that much of it.

540
00:47:54,918 --> 00:48:09,127
[SPEAKER_14]: I think it's one thing that I sometimes think about the Neighborways concept is I like the idea of providing more comfortable, easier, quieter

541
00:48:10,258 --> 00:48:13,720
[SPEAKER_14]: safer routes for people to bypass those major streets.

542
00:48:14,661 --> 00:48:21,184
[SPEAKER_14]: But I also think that we're short-sighted if that's the only thing we do.

543
00:48:21,845 --> 00:48:24,546
[SPEAKER_14]: Because those major streets are also where the businesses are.

544
00:48:24,986 --> 00:48:28,588
[SPEAKER_14]: There are a lot of destinations just along all of those streets.

545
00:48:29,269 --> 00:48:32,751
[SPEAKER_14]: And those streets are the straight shot to get places.

546
00:48:34,112 --> 00:48:37,674
[SPEAKER_14]: And they are still gonna be faster than meandering through neighborhoods.

547
00:48:38,594 --> 00:48:39,795
[SPEAKER_14]: So I think while we,

548
00:48:41,248 --> 00:48:53,153
[SPEAKER_14]: you know, while we focus on the bypasses, we should also pay some attention to doing what we can to improve conditions on, you know, the straight shot.

549
00:48:53,233 --> 00:48:56,075
[SPEAKER_14]: And we do really know where it is that people want to go.

550
00:48:56,575 --> 00:49:01,797
[SPEAKER_14]: It's the big streets that have lots of cars on them, because those are the places that people want to go.

551
00:49:01,817 --> 00:49:07,980
[SPEAKER_03]: Todd mentioned a few times in the presentation to the

552
00:49:08,417 --> 00:49:17,181
[SPEAKER_03]: traffic commission and to us on the Salem Street project, that there were no parking spaces that were being sacrificed.

553
00:49:17,201 --> 00:49:27,385
[SPEAKER_03]: I was perked up by that and wondering if that is still sort of a priority in that do we have a great resistance

554
00:49:28,299 --> 00:49:38,727
[SPEAKER_03]: by homeowners to losing parking spaces in front of their houses compared to let's say five years ago, I'm noticing a transition there.

555
00:49:38,747 --> 00:49:48,215
[SPEAKER_03]: I mentioned it because my pet project here in West Medford would sacrifice 30 spaces, but they're not being used.

556
00:49:49,056 --> 00:49:55,521
[SPEAKER_03]: So you can say on paper, oh, look at all the parking that we're not gonna have, but since so many parks are anyway,

557
00:49:56,042 --> 00:49:58,944
[SPEAKER_03]: Why not put a bike lane in and maybe nobody will complain.

558
00:49:59,524 --> 00:50:03,867
[SPEAKER_03]: But the vibe, you know, your feet are on the ground in a different place.

559
00:50:04,168 --> 00:50:12,693
[SPEAKER_03]: Do you still hear about the great hazards of sacrificing vehicular parking from your end?

560
00:50:13,514 --> 00:50:14,755
[SPEAKER_04]: That's a question for me.

561
00:50:15,327 --> 00:50:16,627
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, Amy.

562
00:50:17,387 --> 00:50:20,908
[SPEAKER_04]: I think so that there is still some resistance.

563
00:50:21,228 --> 00:50:32,570
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you know, so, so we're trying to get routes like, like we prioritize metrics where the new Green Line station other routes, and whenever there's an opportunity that comes up or repaving right.

564
00:50:34,090 --> 00:50:41,832
[SPEAKER_04]: So the only true test so far has been that West Medford safer school project where we eliminate one whole side, and that was all residential.

565
00:50:42,192 --> 00:50:44,132
[SPEAKER_04]: We haven't had a true test in Medford yet.

566
00:50:44,718 --> 00:50:47,420
[SPEAKER_04]: of a residential slash business area.

567
00:50:47,820 --> 00:50:49,722
[SPEAKER_04]: So like a Main Street or Salem Street.

568
00:50:50,302 --> 00:50:57,647
[SPEAKER_04]: So the reason that I specified the Salem, no parking loss is we're trying to get the low hanging fruit first.

569
00:50:58,267 --> 00:51:03,231
[SPEAKER_04]: And then as we go once it's in and they see more bicyclists, the hope is that

570
00:51:04,362 --> 00:51:13,913
[SPEAKER_04]: You know, then if you build it they will come and then people will start to realize, because right now, obviously they say nobody's using it it's not needed you heard some of the people at the traffic commission meeting.

571
00:51:14,514 --> 00:51:18,659
[SPEAKER_04]: So, so, you know, we're doing both when you know, winter street.

572
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:31,051
[SPEAKER_04]: We're likely going to propose removing parking so it doesn't mean we're not going to it just means, just like bus lanes things like that, maybe a little more incremental approach.

573
00:51:31,311 --> 00:51:34,635
[SPEAKER_04]: We're trying to get as much lane as many lanes out there as possible.

574
00:51:35,756 --> 00:51:42,480
[SPEAKER_04]: that are, you know, that are, there's less friction about or anticipated to be less friction.

575
00:51:42,860 --> 00:51:46,983
[SPEAKER_04]: I did not anticipate the friction at Salem Street at all because of the no parking loss.

576
00:51:47,523 --> 00:51:51,425
[SPEAKER_04]: And we still got, you know, feedback saying they didn't like it for whatever reason.

577
00:51:52,506 --> 00:51:59,670
[SPEAKER_04]: So, and it's going to be probably a case by case basis some of the residential neighborhoods that have low parking uses you're pointing out.

578
00:52:01,078 --> 00:52:03,939
[SPEAKER_04]: And he's done a great job collecting a ton of parking data.

579
00:52:04,340 --> 00:52:07,981
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's what helped push that high street West Medford project over the edge.

580
00:52:09,162 --> 00:52:14,464
[SPEAKER_04]: So like some in that master review, we're saying, why not bike lane in both directions?

581
00:52:14,704 --> 00:52:18,546
[SPEAKER_04]: And then some of the community were saying, why not keep parking lanes in both sides?

582
00:52:18,846 --> 00:52:20,967
[SPEAKER_04]: So the compromise was the one in one, right?

583
00:52:20,987 --> 00:52:25,309
[SPEAKER_04]: The uphill in the, so that may be the way it shakes out.

584
00:52:25,329 --> 00:52:29,691
[SPEAKER_04]: It's just, I don't have a crystal ball, but a lot of these residential neighborhoods, it may be,

585
00:52:30,856 --> 00:52:46,348
[SPEAKER_04]: The way it shakes out is one side might be comfortable enough if we show the parking data supports it, in some cases, both sides, but then there might be some downtown districts, a business on each side of the street that may be admirably opposed to any parking loss, so.

586
00:52:47,008 --> 00:52:53,173
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I fully realize these things will perhaps follow an 80-20 rule, but we don't want the tail wagging the dog.

587
00:52:53,732 --> 00:52:57,234
[SPEAKER_14]: You know, just to move things along.

588
00:52:57,274 --> 00:52:59,855
[SPEAKER_14]: Can we go to Peter and then Pat and then be Dan?

589
00:52:59,875 --> 00:53:01,436
[SPEAKER_14]: I know you've been waiting for a little while.

590
00:53:03,517 --> 00:53:04,537
[SPEAKER_11]: Yeah, sure.

591
00:53:08,459 --> 00:53:19,724
[SPEAKER_11]: I was going to kind of Emily echo your point on the neighbor ways, which is what was happening when I raised my hand to say that while they will be helpful for some people who are

592
00:53:21,670 --> 00:53:27,934
[SPEAKER_11]: looking for a safer route, a more comfortable route, and they're definitely a band-aid of sorts.

593
00:53:28,214 --> 00:53:32,417
[SPEAKER_11]: The real problem is going to be that the destinations for people on bikes are the same as on cars.

594
00:53:32,457 --> 00:53:44,264
[SPEAKER_11]: And if we want to have transportation equity and people on bikes being as comfortable moving around the city as people on cars, we're going to have to, at some point, reckon with that.

595
00:53:45,505 --> 00:53:45,805
[SPEAKER_11]: And then,

596
00:53:47,927 --> 00:54:07,954
[SPEAKER_11]: in terms of projects in my particular corner of Medford, tying in the bike lanes on the Wellington Bridge and just the Wellington Bridge bike lanes, which were very nice when they got installed and are getting more and more full of sand and gunk and car parts as the days go on.

597
00:54:10,776 --> 00:54:16,698
[SPEAKER_11]: And I know that's not, that's MassDOT and Somerville and not entirely within the city of Medford's control, but it's just something that affects

598
00:54:17,630 --> 00:54:23,216
[SPEAKER_11]: me and my semi daily life so yeah, Emily should I respond or.

599
00:54:23,917 --> 00:54:24,438
[SPEAKER_14]: Sure, good.

600
00:54:25,138 --> 00:54:29,223
[SPEAKER_04]: Just quickly on those who 20 bridge 20 bike lanes over the bridge.

601
00:54:29,663 --> 00:54:38,173
[SPEAKER_04]: So it's still not complete that grant this remaining work to get you off of the road and onto the path network on the Medford side.

602
00:54:39,507 --> 00:54:48,931
[SPEAKER_04]: Some of those committed to doing that work with one of their contractors, but they have so many other projects going on that we're trying to get scheduled in the course of that.

603
00:54:48,951 --> 00:54:51,712
[SPEAKER_04]: So there's still remaining work there to help folks.

604
00:54:52,492 --> 00:55:02,096
[SPEAKER_04]: Where transitions from the bike lane into the shero and the right turn lane into station landing, there's going to be a pull off into the grass there that you could go directly to the paths.

