[SPEAKER_02]: That'll be three to seven o'clock.

1155
01:50:06,498 --> 01:50:12,619
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's more of a tabling thing, although we could do more if we had an activity.

1156
01:50:13,879 --> 01:50:31,222
[SPEAKER_02]: But I think what we're gonna do is partner up with Walk Medford and Bike to the Sea, which is the organization that got the Northern Strand Trail up through Everett up to Lynn done.

1157
01:50:32,817 --> 01:50:39,039
[SPEAKER_02]: And the kind of theme that we've been talking about is like how to get places.

1158
01:50:39,479 --> 01:50:53,202
[SPEAKER_02]: So it actually works very much into what we've been talking about tonight is like, you know, how to show maybe showing people like how to get from the farmers market to Wellington Circle or

1159
01:50:55,163 --> 01:50:56,965
[SPEAKER_02]: to Arlington Center.

1160
01:50:58,666 --> 01:51:18,684
[SPEAKER_02]: And I think like one thing that we could do is maybe if anybody has like kind of unusual bikes that they might want to bring, like an e-bike or a cargo bike or a classic bike, that could be a kind of fun thing to like demonstrate some of the things that you can do to different kinds of bikes.

1161
01:51:18,844 --> 01:51:20,926
[SPEAKER_02]: Really, really focused on the cargo bike.

1162
01:51:23,193 --> 01:51:25,435
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, well, we'll bring it along.

1163
